   "text": {
    "L1": "An isosceles triangle has two equal sides.",
    "L2": "The equal angles are opposite those equal sides, so they are the two base angles.",
    "L3": "For triangle XYZ, XY equals XZ. Therefore angle Y equals angle Z.",
    "L4": "To see why, join the apex X to the midpoint of the base.",
    "L5": "The two smaller triangles have equal sides, equal half-bases, and a shared line.",
    "L6": "They are congruent by SSS, so their matching base angles are equal.",
    "L7": "The angle sum then finds the remaining angle.",
    "L8": "For example, if each base angle is 52 degrees, angle X is 76 degrees."
   },
